step_details.raw_response:
Thought: Reduce redundancy in the full pool to obtain a cleaner set of models before combining.  
Action: prune_redundant  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","corr_threshold":0.95,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: A robust median on the pruned pool of 8 models may outperform the current weighted baseline, especially given unstable rankings and high correlation.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool4","rationale":"robust median on pruned pool"}

Thought: Ranking is unstable, so a stable subset may yield better performance.  
Action: select_stable  
Action Input: {"k":7}

Thought: The current leader uses a meta‑model weight on the full pool; perhaps a simpler inverse‑error weighting on the pruned, correlated‑error‑reduced pool (pool4) will give a sharper, more robust estimate.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool4","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.0}

Thought: Test inverse-error weighting on the pruned pool (pool4) to see if it can beat the baseline weighted w1.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool4","weights":"w2","rationale":"inverse_error weighting on pruned pool may reduce variance and improve over baseline weighted w1"}

Thought: The current leader uses a pooled meta‑model weight (w1). A series‑specific meta‑model might capture the particular error patterns better. Let's compute a new meta‑model weight for the full pool and evaluate it.  
Action: weights_meta_model  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","scope":"series","metric":"smape","eta":1.0}

Thought: Use inverse‑error weighting on the pruned pool (pool4) but shrink the weights toward uniform to reduce over‑fitting to the few validation windows.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool4","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.5}

Thought: The error correlation is high (mean_corr 0.875) and the ranking is unstable; pruning redundant models should reduce noise and improve a weighted combination.  
Action: prune_redundant  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","corr_threshold":0.95,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: The ranking is unstable and many models are correlated, so a robust median on a stable subset should beat the current weighted baseline.  
Action: select_stable  
Action Input: {"k":7}

Thought: Create a handle for inverse‑error weighting on the stable pool2 and evaluate it; then create a forward‑selection weight handle on the full pool and evaluate that. These should give robust combinations for the noisy, trend‑dominated series.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool2","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.0}  

Thought: Evaluate the inverse‑error weighted combination on pool2.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"w6","rationale":"inverse‑error weights on the stable pool"}  

Thought: Create a forward‑selection weight handle on the full pool.  
Action: weights_forward  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","max_steps":20,"metric":"rmse"}  

Thought: Evaluate the forward‑selection weighted combination on the full pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w7","rationale":"forward‑selection weights on full pool"}

Thought: Evaluate a weighted combination on the stable, pruned pool (pool2) using the inverse‑error weights we already computed (w6) to see if it beats the baseline weighted w1.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"w6","rationale":"test inverse-error weighted on pruned stable pool"}  

Thought: Create a second weight vector on pool2 with moderate shrinkage (0.5) to reduce variance and potentially improve robustness.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool2","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.5}  

Thought: Evaluate the shrinkage‑weighted combination on pool2 to determine if it outperforms the previous weighted and baseline strategies.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"w7","rationale":"test shrinkage-weighted on stable pool"}

Thought: Try the meta‑model weights (w4) on the pruned stable pool (pool2) to see if we can beat the current best weighted w1.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"w4","rationale":"meta‑model weights on pruned stable pool"}

Thought: The series is noisy with unstable model ranking and high error correlation, so a robust inverse‑error weighted mean over the full pool (strategy a10) is the best choice.  
Action: accept  
Action Input: {"id":"a10"}

